// Axis delta: texture .halftone — a geometric PATTERN rather than a grain.
//
// Same primitive as paper or linen; what separates a pattern from a grain
// is only that its structure is meant to read, so it carries more alpha and
// fewer repeats. That is why `pattern` cost nothing once `texture` existed,
// and why it was worth counting them as one gap rather than two.
let l0_texture   = "halftone"
let l0_texture_a = 0.09
let l0_texture_s = 8
